From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 08:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add DataGridView editing-control cluster (clean subset)

Closes the self-contained part of API-COMPLETENESS.md P1 item 2:
IDataGridViewEditingControl (the interface a custom editing control implements),
DataGridViewTextBoxEditingControl (: TextBox) and DataGridViewComboBoxEditingControl
(: ComboBox) implementing it, and DataGridViewTopLeftHeaderCell
(: DataGridViewColumnHeaderCell). These derive from existing controls, so no
re-parenting was needed - a custom DataGridView editing control can now be
written against the real names.

The editing controls round-trip the formatted value through the control's Text,
track row index / value-changed, route the caret/drop-down input keys, and apply
a cell style's font/colours. DataGridViewBand and DataGridViewElement remain
deferred: they are base classes of Row/Column/Cell (which do not currently derive
from them), so adding them is the same re-parenting risk as the section-2 finding.

Covered by DataGridViewEditingControlFunctionalTests. Full Forms suite green at
2487.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
